# Multi-Model Challenge Council + Advisory Triad

**STANDING DIRECTIVE (Tristan 2026-07-29, refined 2026-08-01 from in-anger record):** Do not rely on a single model’s self-assessment. Convene multi-model challenge regularly — and **route by role**, not by “ask the smartest model.”

**Single source of truth for model ids:** `scripts/lib/model_routing.py`  
**Facade imported by FE councils:** `scripts/lib/council_models.py` (must stay locked to routing — `--selftest`)

## Physics ceiling (structural — read before trusting any LLM on EM)

| Benchmark | Reality |
|---|---|
| **CritPt** (research physics) | World-best ≈ **32%** — two-thirds of research-level physics wrong |
| **GPQA Diamond** | Saturated ~92–94% — **does not discriminate**; never pick models on GPQA |

**Consequence:** No LLM is a **validator** for magnetics / electromagnetics / hard physics. Models are **hypothesis generators** and **method reviewers**. Validation stays in **xfemm / solvers / gate registry / proveCatch / twin artefacts**.

**Worse — anti-correlation:** physics skill and non-hallucination honesty pull apart. GPT-5.6 Sol leads CritPt and is among the **worst** at admitting ignorance (~18% non-hallucination). Never accept Sol domain advice unchecked.

