## When to convene

| Cadence | Action |
|---|---|
| After every load-bearing numeric claim | MiniMax (or Qwen long-ctx) evidence check |
| After substantive physics / PCB / morphology milestone | Grok diagnose on digest |
| Before DEC-* freeze / “ready for HoT” / stuck in self-green | Full Grok+Sol+MiniMax council |
| Hard EM / magnetics disagreement (analytic vs FE vs back-EMF) | Sol code/method review **then** solver re-run — Sol never closes the gate |
| Pre-commit on arithmetic / claim patches | `council_precommit_review.py` (uses `model_routing`) |

## How

1. Feed a **digest of delivered artefacts** (twin JSON, solver outputs, PNGs) — SIGHT, not intent alone.
2. Ask **role-appropriate** questions (diagnose ≠ code review ≠ evidence audit).
3. Merge punchlist; fix at **SOURCE** + proveCatch; re-challenge.
4. Harden parsers: truncated JSON, keep-alive padding, reasoning-without-JSON.

